    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0162" n="152" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg152"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.G1/30: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hamilton</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Beck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton, Bermuda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-18T21:00:00-04:00">April 18, 1943—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 19—12:26 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>113. From Dodds for Long and Atherton.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d117-f1"/>
                    Congressman Bloom believes that the question of Polish-Jewish refugees in Russia
                    should be brought up but not determined sometime before end of Conference. He
                    feels that delegation should be able to reply in the affirmative if query made
                    on this point by press or interested parties upon conclusion of Conference.
                    Please instruct. [Dodds.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beck</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d117-f1" n="24" xml:id="d117-f1-content">
                <p>Ray Atherton, Acting Chief of the Division of European Affairs.</p>
            </note>
